# Step by step nav

Publishing step-by-step navigation connects an ordered end-to-end journey across guidance and services. It is not a task-completion tracker. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/step-by-step-nav/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use the navigational structure for a documented setup journey with a real beginning and end: understand requirements, install, then verify. Keep optional or unordered household chores in a task list instead. Opening a guidance step does not mean it has been completed.

## Structure and behaviour

Number genuinely ordered stages and keep their action links visible. Explain prerequisites and optional branches in text. If disclosure controls shorten a long overview, the same headings and links must remain usable without JavaScript. Each destination must stand alone for direct visitors.

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme does not store progress through this reference journey. Do not reuse the step design as an automation status display or assert that an installation succeeded. A service needing saved completion belongs to an explicit task-list implementation.

